 /*
    As we see in this macro language example from DTs manual, sometimes these "do nothing"
    lines actually are commands for the character to say something.

        // Outputs 1, 5, 6, and 11. Your character will say each result aloud
        // (i.e. in a plain text bubble).
        f8
        {
          set num 1  // the value of ‘num’ is now 1
          num "\r"
          set num + 4  // adds 4 to ‘num’, which is now 5
          num "\r"
          set num2 6  // ‘num2’ has the value 6
          num2 "\r"
          set num + num2  // adds 6 to num, yielding 11
          num "\r"
        }
        
        These also can be broken up over multiple lines:
        
        "grfem"
        {
          "Hello fair lady "
          @text         // @text is the complete text in the typing box when the macro started (minus the expression of an expression macro).
          "!\r"
        }
    */
	
	message "This message is strange /r really strange"	// really strange will be ignored

	set arg arg1 + arg2	// only set <arg0> <arg1> and set <arg> .op. <arg1> forms allowed. Can not do arithmetic likes this
